# CakePHP Notification Plugin

## Documentation First

Prefer Notification package docs (`plugins/Notification/docs/index.md` or the package docs in the installed plugin) and Ignis project guidelines before inventing notification wiring. This skill orients you — the package docs hold channel-specific and UI details.

## Installation

```bash
composer require crustum/notification
```

```bash
{{ assist.cakeCommand('plugin load Crustum/Notification') }}
{{ assist.cakeCommand('manifest install --plugin Crustum/Notification') }}
{{ assist.cakeCommand('migrations migrate -p Crustum/Notification') }}
```

Manifest creates `config/notification.php`, copies migrations, and appends config loading in bootstrap.

## Generating Notifications

```bash
{{ assist.cakeCommand('bake notification InvoicePaid') }}
{{ assist.cakeCommand('bake notification InvoicePaid --channels database,mail,slack') }}
```

Classes live under `src/Notification/`. Each defines `via()` plus channel methods (`toMail()`, `toDatabase()`, …).

## Making Entities Notifiable

Use **both** the trait on the table and the behavior:

@ignissnippet("Notifiable UsersTable", "php")
namespace App\Model\Table;

use Cake\ORM\Table;
use Crustum\Notification\Model\Trait\NotifiableTrait;

class UsersTable extends Table
{
    use NotifiableTrait;

    public function initialize(array $config): void
    {
        parent::initialize($config);
        $this->addBehavior('Crustum/Notification.Notifiable');
    }
}
@endignissnippet

@ignissnippet("Send via table notify", "php")
use App\Notification\InvoicePaid;

$usersTable = $this->getTableLocator()->get('Users');
$user = $usersTable->get(1);
$usersTable->notify($user, new InvoicePaid($invoice));
@endignissnippet

Or bulk-send:

@ignissnippet("NotificationManager send", "php")
use Crustum\Notification\NotificationManager;
use App\Notification\InvoicePaid;

NotificationManager::send($users, new InvoicePaid($invoice));
NotificationManager::sendNow($developers, new DeploymentCompleted($deployment));
@endignissnippet

## Channels

Core `crustum/notification` ships **built-in** channels: `mail` and `database`.

Other channel names (`broadcast`, `slack`, `seven`, `telegram`, `rocketchat`, `webhook`) require **additional Composer packages**. Returning them from `via()` without installing the matching plugin will not deliver.

`via()` may return any registered channel name (built-in, optional plugins, or custom):

@ignissnippet("via channels", "php")
public function via(EntityInterface|AnonymousNotifiable $notifiable): array
{
    return $notifiable->prefers_sms ? ['seven'] : ['mail', 'database'];
}
@endignissnippet

### Additional channel plugins

Install only the packages you need. Details live in Notification `docs/modules.md` (and each package’s own docs).

| Channel | Package | Notes |
|---------|---------|--------|
| `broadcast` | `crustum/notification-broadcasting` | Real-time; needs Broadcasting (+ BlazeCast or Mercure). Optional UI: `crustum/notification-ui`. Mercure driver: `crustum/mercure-broadcasting`. |
| `slack` | `crustum/notification-slack` | Plugin `Crustum/SlackNotification`; `toSlack()` |
| `seven` | `crustum/notification-seven` (Seven.io SMS) | `toSeven()`; configure Seven API credentials |
| `telegram` | `crustum/notification-telegram` | `toTelegram()` / media helpers; bot token |
| `rocketchat` | `crustum/notification-rocketchat` | `toRocketchat()`; webhook URL |
| `webhook` | `crustum/notification-webhook` | Arbitrary HTTP endpoints |

Related UI (not a delivery channel): `crustum/notification-ui` — bell/panel for database notifications; optional WebSocket via broadcasting-notification.

After requiring a channel package, load its plugin (and run manifest install when the package provides one), then implement the matching `to*()` method on the notification class.

### Mail

@ignissnippet("toMail MailMessage", "php")
use Crustum\Notification\Message\MailMessage;

public function toMail(EntityInterface|AnonymousNotifiable $notifiable): MailMessage
{
    $url = \Cake\Routing\Router::url(
        ['controller' => 'Invoices', 'action' => 'view', $this->invoice->id],
        true
    );

    return MailMessage::create()
        ->greeting('Hello!')
        ->line('One of your invoices has been paid!')
        ->action('View Invoice', $url)
        ->line('Thank you for using our application!');
}
@endignissnippet

Override recipient with entity `routeNotificationForMail()`. Default subject is the class name in Title Case unless `subject()` is set.

### Database

Prefer `toDatabase()` with `DatabaseMessage`, or `toArray()` for a plain JSON payload:

@ignissnippet("toDatabase DatabaseMessage", "php")
use Crustum\Notification\Message\DatabaseMessage;
use Crustum\Notification\Message\Action;

public function toDatabase(EntityInterface|AnonymousNotifiable $notifiable): DatabaseMessage
{
    return DatabaseMessage::new()
        ->title('Order Shipped')
        ->message('Your order #' . $this->order->id . ' has been shipped')
        ->type('success')
        ->actionUrl(['controller' => 'Orders', 'action' => 'view', $this->order->id])
        ->icon('truck')
        ->addAction(
            Action::new('view')
                ->label('View Order')
                ->url(['controller' => 'Orders', 'action' => 'view', $this->order->id])
                ->type('primary')
        );
}
@endignissnippet

Read/unread helpers on the notifiable table: `unreadNotifications($user)`, `readNotifications($user)`, `markNotificationAsRead($user, $id)`, `markAllNotificationsAsRead($user)`.

## Queueing

Implement `ShouldQueueInterface`. Optional: `delay()`, `$connection`, `$queue`, `viaConnections()`, `viaQueues()`, `shouldSend()`, `afterSending()`.

## On-Demand Recipients

@ignissnippet("AnonymousNotifiable", "php")
use Crustum\Notification\NotificationManager;
use App\Notification\InvoicePaid;

NotificationManager::route('mail', 'taylor@example.com')
    ->route('seven', '5555555555')
    ->route('slack', '#slack-channel')
    ->notify(new InvoicePaid($invoice));
@endignissnippet

## Notification UI and Real-Time

Optional UI: `crustum/notification-ui` + element `Crustum/NotificationUI.notifications/bell_icon`. Real-time needs `crustum/notification-broadcasting` (and usually BlazeCast/Broadcasting or Mercure). Keep database polling as fallback when enabling WebSocket delivery.

## Testing

Use `Crustum\Notification\TestSuite\NotificationTrait` to capture instead of sending. Assert with `assertNotificationSentTo`, `assertNotificationSentToChannel`, `assertNoNotificationsSent`, `assertOnDemandNotificationSent`, etc. Combine with Cake `EmailTrait` for mail body checks.

## Events

- `Model.Notification.sending` — return `false` / stop propagation to cancel
- `Model.Notification.sent`
- `Model.Notification.failed`

## Custom Channels

Implement `ChannelInterface::send()`, register with `NotificationManager::setChannel()` or a `ChannelProviderInterface` on `Notification.Registry.discover`.

## Common Pitfalls

- **Trait without Behavior** — both `NotifiableTrait` and `NotifiableBehavior` are required for table `notify()`.
- **Missing migrations** — database channel needs `migrations migrate -p Crustum/Notification`.
- **Queue without workers** — `ShouldQueueInterface` needs a configured queue and running worker.
- **Mail config** — app email settings drive sender/footer for `MailMessage`.
- **Broadcast / Slack / SMS / … without the channel package** — those channels are optional plugins; see **Additional channel plugins** above.
- **Broadcast channel alone** — also needs Broadcasting (+ server); not enabled by Notification core.
